# Rust
target/

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.json
htmlcov/
lcov.info

# Host secrets / local env (compose reads a repo-root .env; never commit it)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Node (Tauri webview, later)
node_modules/
dist/

# Tauri-generated schemas/bindings (body/app/src-tauri/gen)
gen/

# Harness-local state (session worktrees etc.)
.claude/

# Host-only MCP filesystem sandbox (docs/runbooks/tools-mcp.md)
sandbox/

# Compose bind targets that default into the repo tree. Both are written by root from
# inside a container, and both are unbounded in size: pgdata/ receives the pg-backup
# sidecar's cortex.dump (CORTEX_DB_DIR, docs/runbooks/memory-pgvector.md) and models/ is
# where the GGUFs land when CORTEX_MODELS_DIR is left at its default. Unanchored on
# purpose: a bare docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.memory.yml resolves the binds
# against docker/ rather than the repo root, so docker/pgdata and docker/models are
# reachable too.
pgdata/
models/

# The same second project directory, for the binds that name a repo input rather than an output.
# ./docker/postgres/init.sql and its two neighbours resolve to docker/docker/postgres/... when the
# project directory is docker/, where the repo ships nothing, so compose would create that phantom
# nest instead of finding the file. Anchored, because only the one under docker/ is phantom.
docker/docker/
